# The Five Rooms

The site mirrors the app's theme system. `foolscap` is the default and the fallback for any unrecognized value.

| Room | Mood | Dark bg | Accent |
|------|------|---------|--------|
| `foolscap` | espresso & gold | `#17130F` | `#E8C870` |
| `inkwell` | graphite & indigo | `#14161B` | `#96A8DC` |
| `verdant` | spruce & copper | `#111710` | `#D89A5E` |
| `dusk` | mulberry & rose | `#181218` | `#D6A08A` |
| `harbor` | sea slate & foam | `#0F1517` | `#7AB0A8` |

## Tokens Live in Two Places — Update Both, Every Time

1. `styles.css` — one `html[data-theme="<room>"]` block per room, plus a `:root` Foolscap fallback
2. `theme.js` — the `ROOMS` array, which drives the shelf previews and picker swatches

Changing a color in one and not the other silently desyncs the preview from the page it previews.

Values are copied from the app's `AppColors.swift` / `AppTheme.swatch`. The convention: **page ground = the room's LIGHT mode; phone mockups = the room's DARK mode** — hence the parallel `--d-*` tokens in every block.

## Mechanics

- Applied as `data-theme` on `<html>`, persisted in `localStorage` under `musing-theme`
- Every page carries an **inline `<head>` script** that reads localStorage and sets `data-theme` before first paint. Omit it and the page flashes Foolscap before correcting.
- The room regex is duplicated into that inline script on every page: `/^(foolscap|inkwell|verdant|dusk|harbor)$/`. Adding a room means updating it on **every** page plus both files above.
- `theme.js` exposes `window.MusingTheme = { ROOMS, setTheme, storedTheme }`

## Adding a Page

Include the inline theme script, `/styles.css`, `/theme.js`, and the `.picker` swatch markup (or `.doc-top` for document-style pages). Use root-relative paths — `index.html` uses bare `styles.css` only because it sits at the root.

## Gotchas

- Use CSS custom properties for color. Hardcoded hex outside the theme blocks won't transition when the room changes (`background`/`color` transitions run at `.5s ease`).
- `setTheme` maintains `aria-pressed` on swatches and the `.active` class on swatches and minis — don't hand-manage either.
- Parenthesize a template string before `.repeat()`; string-concat vs. repeat precedence has already caused one bug in `renderShelf`.
